## Configuration Management

- Manage configuration changes with chezmoi. Before editing a configuration file, check whether it is managed with `chezmoi source-path <target>`.
- For a managed file, edit its chezmoi source rather than only its deployed target, then apply the targeted change with `chezmoi apply <target>` and verify it with `chezmoi diff <target>`.
- When Caden asks to change an unmanaged, non-sensitive configuration file, add it to chezmoi as part of the change. Inspect it first to ensure it contains no secrets or other private data, then use `chezmoi add <target>` and make subsequent edits in the generated source file.
- Do not add credentials, tokens, private keys, network details, or other confidential files to chezmoi.

## Privacy Boundary

This file is tracked in a public chezmoi repository. Never add credentials, API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, IP addresses, hostnames, network topology, physical locations, contact details, family or friend information, private repository details, or other confidential data. Keep system context general and non-identifying.
